        "id": "future-perfect-simple",
        "title": "Future Perfect Simple",
        "icon": "🏁",
        "guide": "## Future Perfect Simple (Kelasi zamon oldindan tugallangan ish-harakat)\n\nFuture Perfect Simple kelajakdagi **ma'lum bir vaqtga qadar** yoki kelajakdagi boshqa bir voqeadan **oldin tugallangan bo'ladigan** ish-harakatni ko'rsatish uchun ishlatiladi.\n\n## 1. Shakllanishi (Form)\n• **Tasdiq**: Subject + will have + V3 (Past Participle)\n  - By next year, I **will have graduated** from university.\n• **Inkor**: Subject + will not (won't) have + V3\n  - He **won't have saved** enough money by next summer.\n• **Savol**: Will + Subject + have + V3?\n  - **Will** you **have finished** your homework before dinner?\n\n*(will barcha shaxs/sonlar uchun bir xil — o'zgarmaydi)*\n\n## 2. Ishlatilishi (Usage)\n1. **Ma'lum kelajakdagi vaqtga qadar tugallangan ish-harakat**:\n   - By 2030, they **will have built** the new bridge.\n2. **Kelajakdagi boshqa voqeadan oldin tugallanadigan ish-harakat**:\n   - She **will have finished** the report **by the time** you arrive.\n3. **Ishonch bilan taxmin qilingan tugallangan holat**:\n   - By now, he **will have arrived** home. (ishonch bilan taxmin)\n\n## 3. Future Perfect Simple vs Future Simple\n• **Future Simple** — kelajakdagi oddiy voqea.\n  - I **will finish** the report tomorrow. (qachon tugashi aniq emas, faqat kelajakda)\n• **Future Perfect Simple** — ma'lum vaqtga QADAR tugallangan bo'lishini ta'kidlaydi.\n  - I **will have finished** the report **by** tomorrow. (ertangi kungacha tugagan bo'ladi)\n\n## 4. Signal so'zlar\n• by, by then, by the time, before, by next week/month/year\n• in + kelajakdagi vaqt (by 2030)",
